LOCUS       TWO_GENE_FIXTURE        1600 bp    DNA     linear   SYN 31-AUG-2026
DEFINITION  Synthetic two-gene locus: a partial CDS precedes the complete one.
ACCESSION   TWO_GENE_FIXTURE
VERSION     TWO_GENE_FIXTURE.1
KEYWORDS    synthetic; fixture; regression test.
SOURCE      synthetic construct
  ORGANISM  synthetic construct
COMMENT     Reproduces the hazard in NCBI RefSeqGene records that annotate a
            neighbouring gene: the FIRST CDS in the file belongs to NEIGHBOURA and
            is partial (<1..70), out of frame and lacks ATG, exactly like TOMM40 in
            NG_007084. TARGETB is the complete gene. Selecting by file order
            designs against the wrong gene; selecting by completeness does not.
            Fully synthetic - no reference, project or subject data.
FEATURES             Location/Qualifiers
     source          1..1600
                     /organism="synthetic construct"
                     /mol_type="other DNA"
     gene            <1..200
                     /gene="NEIGHBOURA"
                     /label="NEIGHBOURA"
     mRNA            join(<1..70,120..200)
                     /gene="NEIGHBOURA"
                     /transcript_id="SYN_NEIGHBOURA.1"
     CDS             <1..70
                     /gene="NEIGHBOURA"
                     /label="NEIGHBOURA CDS"
                     /codon_start=1
     gene            501..1300
                     /gene="TARGETB"
                     /label="TARGETB"
     mRNA            join(501..800,1001..1300)
                     /gene="TARGETB"
                     /transcript_id="SYN_TARGETB.1"
     CDS             join(501..800,1001..1300)
                     /gene="TARGETB"
                     /label="TARGETB CDS"
                     /codon_start=1
     exon            501..800
                     /gene="TARGETB"
                     /label="Exon 1"
     exon            1001..1300
                     /gene="TARGETB"
                     /label="Exon 2"
